Z||000000||otis||02-27-2000||07:12 PM||||Okay,this has been done before,but<BR>I did read all the previous posts and<BR>tried many of the solutions offered to<BR>no avail. I have just put re-built 2.8L<BR>long blocks into both of my 86GTs and<BR>have correct idle speed 800-900 rpms,<BR>but the engines are "hunting" up and down<BR>and this causes a rough idle. One of the<BR>engines does have a weak lifter and the cams<BR>are both re-grinds as the local rebuilder<BR>does  not install new camshafts. I have<BR>checked for vacuum leaks including the<BR>EGR, various lines. The only place that I<BR>can't check is the lifter valley below the<BR>lower intake manifold. The only conclusive<BR>thing I could find was a low fuel  pressure<BR>reading at the fuel rail. This resulted in<BR>me having to replace all cylinder injectors<BR>for one of the engines. Has anyone had this<BR>same problem and gone through the usual <BR>troubleshooting and found a root cause?<BR>The only other thing I did find was that<BR>the pressure still did not hold very good<BR>on the 86 auto  and this might me the fuel<BR>pressure regualtor. Maybe both of these are<BR>going out and causing this problem. Any ideas<BR>are appreciated and  will be tried as I have<BR>run out go do's  other change cams and lifters and redo lower intake manifold gaskets in the event of lifter valley vacuum<BR>leak.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||02-28-2000||04:00 AM||||I've never had this problem but the book I have mentions the MAP sensor as a possible, and easy to check, just unplug and see if idle stabilizes (about the only thing you didn't mention by name as having tried already).  Bad grounds can also cause erratic idle, but that's too easy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sdm1964||02-28-2000||06:56 AM||||I know the feeling, my 85 GT does the same thing, hunts at idle, not rought just up and down, seems to stabilize if you turn on the A/C. I have put in new plugs , wires, cap, fuel filter, checked timing, etc, etc. The lights flicker at idle too, just learned to live with it. The alt, came from my Z28 and worked fine, I am thinking of cleaning all the grounds etc to see if i can make it any better. Good luck||||reg||9
Z||000003||Bens88GT||02-28-2000||11:44 PM||||I had the same problem since I got my car two weeks ago. I replaced the EGR valve, PCV valve, distributor cap and rotor, to no avail. Turns out it was the IAC (Idle Air Control valve). You'll know it's this valve if your engine sometimes idles steadily, then you hear a "clink" sound from the engine, and it suddenly starts hunting and dropping RPMs. Hope this helps.||||reg||3
